   "reason": "The scope3 per-native observers learn DELETE (dev3-row-delete.md#implementation-2b3); they stay test-only oracles with no product caller (product code only names status.rs's unchanged StatementBoundary type). status.rs moves Status for DeleteForward/DeleteClr/DeletePrune by their INSERT role (Commit and the Prune role take the commit Q). undo.rs binds the selected Job's effect to the opcode (IdentityMismatch otherwise, the 2b-1 transition rule; defence in depth, since the opcode's native size rule, U 432 B or 432+L B, refuses a mismatched frame first) and reads an effect-1 root's U through entry (b): Live 432+L with a RowValue Committed/logical/Inline before, Releasing 432 B with no payload and no before stamp from cursor 3; the one-slot Undo page check now takes a cell ending at INITIAL_UNDO_CELL's end of at least 432 B, and the H proof over a DELETE predecessor uses the same entry (b) against its Job. leaf.rs checks the leaf reservation before (entries + D <= 16188, Corrupt) and after the group with DELETE's C-180 change of D (OrderMismatch), types every row (a tombstone only with a Transaction stamp and its U), checks the actor's record (tombstone 180 B for DELETE) and, for DeleteForward/DeleteClr/DeletePrune, the committed old or restored row against U's Live before read through entry (a) with the table schema and U's Releasing after byte-for-byte. The N1 cross-check drops the effect-1 and DELETE-opcode skips: status/undo/jobs observe every history D group, and leaf.rs joins it for the first time (the World encodes the table's Catalog record and keeps each produced RowReserve's sealed value) over the 15 groups that change the leaf; A's three literal INSERT Forwards have no sealed value in this World and are covered by A's literal comparison. For each of the six DELETE groups a rebound candidate with U's before logical +1 is accepted by undo.rs (entry (b)) and refused by leaf.rs (IdentityMismatch: the old row at DeleteForward, the Releasing after at DeleteClr/DeletePrune); at the DeleteClr, a candidate with the restored row's logical +1 and the core's after projection rewritten to match is refused by leaf.rs's comparison with U's Live before; at the four groups whose H is a DELETE predecessor, the H page's U with its incoming count +1 (page digest resealed) is refused by undo.rs's entry-(b) H proof (IdentityMismatch; an edit of that root's Job would break its budget and be refused by the Job codec first). Each of these mutants fails its case in a build with its target check disabled. RDL-C: a DeleteForward of another RowId (D-524's tombstone key and row 2 -> 3, rebound) is refused by C's observer (Corrupt) and leaf.rs (IdentityMismatch). The status/undo/leaf unit cases (status_tests.rs, undo_tests.rs, leaf_tests.rs, unchanged) and the N1/S1 cases keep the INSERT observations unchanged.",
